{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"Usually, there are many different ways to divide polynomials. Here, we will use the method of polynomial long division.\n\nNotice that the expression in the numerator is missing a $2^{\\text{nd}}$ degree term. To avoid any confusion, let's add that term as $0x^2$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{array}{r}\n3x^2\\phantom{+4x-11}\n\\\\\nx+1|\\overline{3x^3+0x^2+\\phantom{3}x-11}\n\\\\\n\\mathllap{-(}\\underline{3x^3+3x^2\\phantom{+3x-11}\\rlap )}\n\\\\\n{}-3x^2+\\phantom{0}x-11\n\\end{array}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{array}{r}\n3x^2-3x\\phantom{+11}\n\\\\\nx+1|\\overline{3x^3+0x^2+\\phantom{3}x-11}\n\\\\\n\\mathllap{-(}\\underline{3x^3+3x^2\\phantom{+3x-11}\\rlap )}\n\\\\\n{}-3x^2+\\phantom{0}x-11\n\\\\\n\\mathllap{-(}\\underline{{}-3x^2-3x\\phantom{-11}\\rlap )}\n\\\\\n4x-11\n\\end{array}$","images":{},"replace":true,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{array}{r}\n3x^2-3x+\\phantom{1}4\n\\\\\nx+1|\\overline{3x^3+0x^2+\\phantom{3}x-11}\n\\\\\n\\mathllap{-(}\\underline{3x^3+3x^2\\phantom{+3x-11}\\rlap )}\n\\\\\n{}-3x^2+\\phantom{0}x-11\n\\\\\n\\mathllap{-(}\\underline{{}-3x^2-3x\\phantom{-11}\\rlap )}\n\\\\\n4x-11\n\\\\\n\\mathllap{-(}\\underline{4x+\\phantom{1}4\\rlap )}\n\\\\\n-15\n\\end{array}$","images":{},"replace":true,"widgets":{}},{"content":"We found that the quotient is $3x^2-3x+4$ and the remainder is $-15$:\n\n$\\dfrac{3x^3+x-11}{x+1}=3x^2-3x+4-\\dfrac{15}{x+1}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Divide the polynomials.**  \n*The form of your answer should either be $p(x)$ or $p(x)+\\dfrac{k}{x+1}$ where $p(x)$ is a polynomial and $k$ is an integer.*\n\n$\\dfrac{3x^3+x-11}{x+1}=$ [[☃ expression 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerFo